CloudBurrow patch 15 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1277). Needs googlesqlite patch 0028.

The bug: a table made by tables.insert with timePartitioning and no
field (an ingestion-time partitioned table) was made in the engine as
any other table (contentdata's CreateTable), so it kept no row's
ingestion time and _PARTITIONTIME and _PARTITIONDATE could not be read
from it. Measured through CloudBurrow's front, 2026-10-15.

BigQuery keeps each row's ingestion time, truncated to the partitioning
unit, whatever writes it (DML, tabledata.insertAll, a load, the Storage
Write API) (https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/querying-partitioned-tables).
The patch makes such a table with PARTITION BY
TIMESTAMP_TRUNC(_PARTITIONTIME, <its type>), which gives it the
pseudo-columns (googlesqlite patch 0028); every write leaves them out of
its INSERT, so the engine fills them in. It also leaves the
pseudo-columns out of the schema of a table made by CREATE TABLE ...
PARTITION BY _PARTITIONDATE (addTableMetadata).
server/ingestion_partition_test.go fails without the patch and passes
with it.

